  "notes": "The 1999–2001 revival board, and the research's comparison is the parameter: bouncier and busier than 1993 Death Row. That is the highest `tresilloBias` and `offbeat8thShare` of the LA entries here, a rimshot layer with the busiest ghost-note field in the batch — four positions at a real probability — and tambourine on the 8ths. He came out of the George Clinton orbit before hip-hop, so the harmony is played dominant-7/minor-9 vamp material rather than one-finger synth lines: sevenths and ninths take three quarters of the extension mass over two-chord vamps. His documented job on the out-of-region album was to add synth bass, a high saw lead and female backing vocals, which is exactly the three parts this entry overrides — melody sits higher than any other entry here at 76–100 for the saw, the countermelody is `octave_echo` for the stacked backing voices, and the bass is played with rests and pushed 16ths, hence `anticipationProb` 0.45 against a mid `followRootsProb`. ⚠ `medium` is the research's own rating; the band background and the album brief are documented, the drum and harmony numbers are read from the records.",
